   "t": 840,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp2bppp/2np1n2/2p1p3/2B1P3/2NP1N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQ1RK1 w kq - 7 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "The older path was a knight to g5, short castles, f4 — still popular today.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 842.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1rk1/pp2bppp/2np1n2/2p1p1N1/2B1PP2/2NP4/PPP3PP/R1BQ1RK1 b - - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "Ng5",
    "O-O",
    "f4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 4,
   "t": 849.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/2p5/4P3/2N5/PPPP1PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 2 3",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 851,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 4 4",
   "line": [
    "Nb1",
    "Nb8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 854.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/8/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "d4",
    "cxd4",
    "Qxd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "The queen recapture on d4 isn't the most testing, but if White follows up accurately you need to know what to do.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 868,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": "A knight to c6 — and although a queen to d1 is most popular...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 871,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/4P3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [
    "Qd1"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 872.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 6 8",
   "line": [
    "Nd4",
    "Qd2",
    "Nc6",
    "Qd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...the only testing continuation is a queen to d3, which Shimanov likes with White. You have to quickly go e6 and d5 to equalize.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 889.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppppp/2n2n2/8/4P3/3Q4/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 8 9",
   "line": [
    "Nf6",
    "Qd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The computer says play a knight to f6; Shimanov goes a knight to c3 to prevent d5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 906.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n1pn2/8/4P3/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R1B1KBNR b KQkq - 1 10",
   "line": [
    "e6",
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": "Usually White plays a knight to c3, and you quickly go e6 — the main line is a bishop to f4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 921,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/1p1p1ppp/p1n1pn2/8/4P3/2NQ1N2/PPP2PPP/R1B1KB1R b KQkq - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "a6",
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White plays a knight to f3 instead, you play a6, the typical Sicilian move covering b5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 929,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/1pqp1ppp/p1n1pn2/8/4P3/2NQ1N2/PPP1BPPP/R1B1K2R b KQkq - 3 12",
   "line": [
    "Qc7",
    "Be2"
   ],
   "spoken": "If White skips a bishop to f4, you can put the queen on c7 — what Sicilian does a6 and a queen to c7 remind you of?",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 944,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 4 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "It's like a Kan — e6, a6, then a queen to c7.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 8,
   "t": 945.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1p1ppp/4p3/2p5/4P3/5N2/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [
    "Nf3",
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 948.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/1p1p1ppp/p3p3/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "d4",
    "cxd4",
    "Nxd4",
    "a6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 950,
   "fen": "rnb1kbnr/1pqp1ppp/p3p3/8/3NP3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 2 8",
   "line": [
    "Nc3",
    "Qc7"
   ],
   "spoken": "One of the most reputable Sicilians: you restrict the knight, the queen is safe, and White struggles to develop the dark-squared bishop actively.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 967,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/1p1p1ppp/p3p3/8/3NP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 4 9",
   "line": [
    "Nb1",
    "Qd8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 974.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 4 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 977,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 1 6",
   "line": [
    "d4",
    "cxd4",
    "Qxd4",
    "Nc6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 978.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/4P3/3Q4/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [
    "Qd3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 979.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppppp/2n2n2/8/4P3/3Q4/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR w KQkq - 3 7",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 980.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppppp/2n2n2/8/4P3/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R1B1KBNR b KQkq - 4 7",
   "line": [
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 982,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n1pn2/8/4P3/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 983.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n1pn2/8/4PB2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R3KBNR b KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Bf4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 986,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/1p1p1ppp/p1n1pn2/8/4PB2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R3KBNR w KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "a6"
   ],
   "spoken": "After the bishop to f4, a6 is best, just like in the Magnus Sicilian.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 988,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/1p1p1ppp/p1n1pn2/8/4PB2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR b kq - 1 9",
   "line": [
    "O-O-O"
   ],
   "spoken": "White castles queenside quickly.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 992.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/3p1ppp/p1n1pn2/1p6/4PB2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "b5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And after b5 you get a sharp position the computer calls equal, with excellent queenside counterplay.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 1001.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/3p1ppp/p1n1pn2/1p2P3/5B2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR b kq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black has excellent queenside counterplay — the pawn to e5 here has been played at a high level.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 1007,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/2qp1ppp/p1n1pn2/1p2P3/5B2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "Qc7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The best move seems to be a queen to c7 — if White takes the knight, you take the bishop with check.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 1016,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/2qp1ppp/p1n1pn2/1p2P3/5B2/2N2Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR b kq - 2 11",
   "line": [
    "Qf3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 1018,
   "fen": "r1b1kbnr/2qp1ppp/p1n1p3/1p2P3/5B2/2N2Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 3 12",
   "line": [
    "Ng8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 1023,
   "fen": "r1b1kbnr/2qp1ppp/p1n1p3/1p2P3/5B2/2N3Q1/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR b kq - 4 12",
   "line": [
    "Qg3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 1024,
   "fen": "r3kbnr/1bqp1ppp/p1n1p3/1p2P3/5B2/2N3Q1/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 5 13",
   "line": [
    "Bb7"
   ],
   "spoken": "Against a queen to g3, a bishop to b7 and Black is better; then a rook to c8 and the knight reroutes to g6.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 26,
   "t": 1029.5,
   "fen": "r1b1kbnr/2qp1ppp/p1n1p3/1p2P3/5B2/2N2Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 7 14",
   "line": [
    "Qf3",
    "Bc8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 27,
   "t": 1030.5,
   "fen": "r1b1kbnr/2qp1ppp/p1n1p3/1p2P3/4NB2/5Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR b kq - 8 14",
   "line": [
    "Ne4"
   ],
   "spoken": "White has to know a knight to e4, and you play a bishop to b7 anyway.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 1035.5,
   "fen": "r3kbnr/1bqp1ppp/p1n1p3/1p2P3/4NB2/5Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 9 15",
   "line": [
    "Bb7"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 1040,
   "fen": "r3k1nr/1bqp1ppp/p1nbp3/1p2P3/5B2/5Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 0 16",
   "line": [
    "Nd6+",
    "Bxd6"
   ],
   "spoken": "If a knight check on d6, a bishop capture, the recapture, and a queen to a5 gives a double-edged position I like for Black.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 1041.5,
   "fen": "r3k1nr/1b1p1ppp/p1nPp3/qp6/5B2/5Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 1 17",
   "line": [
    "exd6",
    "Qa5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 34,
   "t": 1048,
   "fen": "r3k2r/1b1p1ppp/p1nPpn2/qp6/5B2/5Q2/PPP2PPP/1K1R1BNR w kq - 3 18",
   "line": [
    "Kb1",
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black is already better — this is Szabo-Ter-Sahakyan, European Championship 2023, which Black won quickly.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 35,
   "t": 1058,
   "fen": "r3k2r/1b1p1ppp/p1nPpn2/qp6/8/5Q2/PPPB1PPP/1K1R1BNR b kq - 4 18",
   "line": [
    "Bd2"
   ],
   "spoken": "A bishop to d2 was played.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 36,
   "t": 1060.5,
   "fen": "r3k2r/1b1p1ppp/p1nPpn2/q7/1p6/5Q2/PPPB1PPP/1K1R1BNR w kq - 0 19",
   "line": [
    "b4"
   ],
   "spoken": "Samvel Ter-Sahakyan played b4.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 38,
   "t": 1064,
   "fen": "r3k2r/1b1p1ppp/p1nPpn2/8/qp6/P4Q2/1PPB1PPP/1K1R1BNR w kq - 1 20",
   "line": [
    "a3",
    "Qa4"
   ],
   "spoken": "a3, a queen to a4 unpinning — White is already in trouble.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 40,
   "t": 1070.5,
   "fen": "r3k2r/1b1p1ppp/p1nP1n2/4p3/qp3Q2/P7/1PPB1PPP/1K1R1BNR w kq - 0 21",
   "line": [
    "Qf4",
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Black won in about seven moves — a queen to f4, e5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 42,
   "t": 1072,
   "fen": "2r1k2r/1b1p1ppp/p1nP1n2/4p3/qpQ5/P7/1PPB1PPP/1K1R1BNR w k - 2 22",
   "line": [
    "Qc4",
    "Rc8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 44,
   "t": 1076,
   "fen": "2r1k2r/1b1p1ppp/p2P1n2/n3p3/qpQ5/P4N2/1PPB1PPP/1K1R1B1R w k - 4 23",
   "line": [
    "Nf3",
    "Na5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 45,
   "t": 1084,
   "fen": "2r1k2r/1b1p1ppp/p2P1n2/n3p3/qp6/P2Q1N2/1PPB1PPP/1K1R1B1R b k - 5 23",
   "line": [
    "Qd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "If the queen goes back to d3...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 46,
   "t": 1087,
   "fen": "2r1k2r/3p1ppp/p2P1n2/n3p3/qp2b3/P2Q1N2/1PPB1PPP/1K1R1B1R w k - 6 24",
   "line": [
    "Be4"
   ],
   "spoken": "...you walk into a bishop or pawn to e4, otherwise you can't save c2 — White ended up giving up the queen.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 1097.5,
   "fen": "r3k1nr/1b1p1ppp/p1nPp3/qp6/5B2/5Q2/PPP2PPP/2KR1BNR w kq - 1 17",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "It looks slow, but White is incredibly undeveloped — a big lead and chances against the king.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 1103.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/4P3/3Q4/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "That's what I'd recommend against a queen to d3: a knight to f6, a knight to c3, e6.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 1106.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n1pn2/8/4P3/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R1B1KBNR w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "Nf6",
    "Nc3",
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "You can also play d5...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 1108,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n1pn2/8/4PB2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R3KBNR b KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Bf4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 1110,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/1p1p1ppp/p1n1pn2/8/4PB2/2NQ4/PPP2PPP/R3KBNR w KQkq - 0 9",
   "line": [
    "a6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...but I like the a6 approach — it keeps more pieces on.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 1124.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/4P3/3Q4/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "As a newer player you'll face a queen to d1 more often than d3.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 1131.5,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/8/3QP3/8/PPP2PPP/RNB1KBNR b KQkq - 0 5",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "After a knight to f6 and a knight to c3, e5 is perfectly fine and e6 is also good.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 1136,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1ppppp/2n2n2/8/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR b KQkq - 4 7",
   "line": [
    "Nc6",
    "Qd1",
    "Nf6",
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 1137,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": "I like e5, because apparently the only way for White to equalize...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 1148,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N5/PPP1NPPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Nge2"
   ],
   "spoken": "...is a knight to e2, which nobody plays in their right mind — computer nonsense.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 1156,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/1b2P3/2N5/PPP1NPPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 2 9",
   "line": [
    "Bb4"
   ],
   "spoken": "A bishop to b4, a3...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 1160,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/b3p3/4P3/P1N5/1PP1NPPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 10",
   "line": [
    "a3",
    "Ba5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 1162,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/b3p3/1P2P3/P1N5/2P1NPPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "b4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 20,
   "t": 1164,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/1bn2n2/4p3/1P2P3/P1N5/2P1NPPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 1 11",
   "line": [
    "Bb6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...a bishop to b6, and White has to find another computer move.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 1170,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/1bn2n2/4p3/1P2P3/P1N4P/2P1NPP1/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 11",
   "line": [
    "h3"
   ],
   "spoken": "If h3 to stop a knight to g4, White is already much worse from the development lead.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 22,
   "t": 1173,
   "fen": "r1bq1k1r/pp1p1ppp/1bn2n2/4p3/1P2P3/P1N4P/2P1NPP1/R1BQKB1R w KQ - 1 12",
   "line": [
    "Kf8"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 1177.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1kr1/pp1p1ppp/1bn2n2/4p3/1P2P3/P1N3NP/2P2PP1/R1BQKB1R w KQ - 3 13",
   "line": [
    "Ng3",
    "Rg8"
   ],
   "spoken": "White's big problem: if the knight moves, you blast open the center with d5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 1179.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1kr1/pp3ppp/1bn2n2/3pp3/1P2P3/P1N3NP/2P2PP1/R1BQKB1R w KQ - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "Nd5",
    "d6",
    "Nc3",
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "After d5 and the capture, there's a very important intermezzo.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 29,
   "t": 1183,
   "fen": "r1bq1kr1/pp3ppp/1bn2n2/3Pp3/1P6/P1N3NP/2P2PP1/R1BQKB1R b KQ - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "exd5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 30,
   "t": 1190.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1kr1/pp3ppp/2n2n2/3Pp3/1P1b4/P1N3NP/2P2PP1/R1BQKB1R w KQ - 1 16",
   "line": [
    "Bd4"
   ],
   "spoken": "A bishop to d4 — this is why b4 in the Sicilian is such a liability, letting the knight be targeted.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 32,
   "t": 1200.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1kr1/pp3ppp/2n5/3np3/1P1b4/P1N3NP/1BP2PP1/R2QKB1R w KQ - 0 17",
   "line": [
    "Bb2",
    "Nxd5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Then a knight capture on d5 with a huge advantage — don't hesitate to sacrifice a pawn to open the center when you lead in development.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 24,
   "t": 1202.5,
   "fen": "r1bq1kr1/pp1p1ppp/1bn2n2/4p3/1P2P3/P1N3NP/2P2PP1/R1BQKB1R w KQ - 3 13",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 28,
   "t": 1204,
   "fen": "r1bq1kr1/pp3ppp/1bn2n2/3pp3/1P2P3/P1N3NP/2P2PP1/R1BQKB1R w KQ - 0 15",
   "line": [
    "Nd5",
    "d6",
    "Nc3",
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Sacrifice a pawn to open up the centre when you have a big lead in development.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 1212.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkbnr/pp1ppppp/2n5/8/4P3/8/PPP2PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 2 6",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 14,
   "t": 1213.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQKBNR w KQkq - 0 8",
   "line": [
    "Nf6",
    "Nc3",
    "e5"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 1214.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [
    "Nf3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The most popular move in the database is a knight to f3, but a bishop to b4 is excellent for Black.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 16,
   "t": 1221,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/1b2P3/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 2 9",
   "line": [
    "Bb4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 1224,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/1b2P3/2NB1N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 3 9",
   "line": [
    "Bd3"
   ],
   "spoken": "For example a bishop to d3, and you play d5, or just castle and take on c3 for a typical Sicilian structure, slightly better for Black.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 1240,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 5 10",
   "line": [
    "Bf8",
    "Bf1"
   ],
   "spoken": "A typical Sicilian structure with a damaged queenside — Black is slightly better; here we faced an outright poor move.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 23,
   "t": 1241.5,
   "fen": "r1bqk2r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/1B2p3/1b2P3/2N5/PPP2PPP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 9 12",
   "line": [
    "Be7",
    "Ng1",
    "Bb4",
    "Bb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "We faced a bad move, a bishop to b5, and after a bishop to b4 White is already in trouble.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 15,
   "t": 1251.5,
   "fen": "r1bqkb1r/pp1p1ppp/2n2n2/4p3/4P3/2N2N2/PPP2PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 1 8",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "In response to a3, Black should just play a bishop to e7, not engaging — then after a knight to e2, expand in the center with c5. White is completely paralyzed: he can't develop, since a knight to h3 walks into a bishop capture. Just castle and expand on the queenside with a5 or c4, clamping down on b2 with a rook to b8 — the computer says plus three, an instructive evaluation because White's position is simply miserable. That's the theme of the whole session: keep a big lead in development, don't autopilot after winning material, and reserve flashy sacrifices for when the position actually demands them — the simple sound move is almost always enough.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 6,
   "t": 2053,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/8/PPPP1PPP/RNBQKBNR w KQkq - 4 4",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "a6 is horrible, and you should have firm intuition to play d5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 7,
   "t": 2054,
   "fen": "rnbqkbnr/pp1ppppp/8/2p5/4P3/2P5/PP1P1PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 4",
   "line": [
    "c3"
   ],
   "spoken": "In the Alapin there's a line newer players fall into...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 2058,
   "fen": "rnb1kbnr/pp2pppp/8/2pq4/3P4/2P5/PP3PPP/RNBQKBNR b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "d5",
    "exd5",
    "Qxd5",
    "d4"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
