   "t": 2063.5,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3q4/3P4/5N2/PP3PPP/RNBQKB1R w KQkq - 3 9",
   "line": [
    "Nf6"
   ],
   "spoken": "...a knight to f6...",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 2065.5,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3q4/3P4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 4 9",
   "line": [
    "Nc3"
   ],
   "spoken": ""
  },
  {
   "ply": 18,
   "t": 2068.5,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/pp1qpppp/2n2n2/8/3P4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R w KQkq - 5 10",
   "line": [
    "Qd7"
   ],
   "spoken": "...and if a queen to d7, Black loses on the spot.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 19,
   "t": 2070,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/pp1qpppp/2n2n2/3P4/8/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 0 10",
   "line": [
    "d5"
   ],
   "spoken": "Same concept — d5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 21,
   "t": 2074,
   "fen": "r1bnkb1r/pp1qpppp/5n2/1B1P4/8/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQK2R b KQkq - 2 11",
   "line": [
    "Nd8",
    "Bb5"
   ],
   "spoken": "And the bishop comes to b5.",
   "reanchor": true
  },
  {
   "ply": 17,
   "t": 2077,
   "fen": "r1b1kb1r/pp2pppp/2n2n2/3q4/3P4/2N2N2/PP3PPP/R1BQKB1R b KQkq - 4 9",
   "line": [],
   "spoken": "You can virtually pre-move d5, because wherever the queen goes it's strong. Then a bishop to f4, not rushing to release the tension, castle queenside. A bishop capture on b5 would be overly flashy and bad — it allows counterplay with a rook capture on a2, and overestimates the c7 threat. Get your priorities straight: the default is the simple move; only check sacrifices when the simple move doesn't work.",
   "reanchor": true
  }
 ]
}